  "observation": "All 27 original decoder returns across Disc 1 fields 23/14 and Disc 2 field 15 match reconstructed output hashes, lengths, input ends and returned destination pointers when given the measured original source memory. The loaded file digest matches its entire measured source slot in each call. Field 23 component 8 reads five bytes beyond the file; four adjacent RAM bytes change output padding at offsets 74..77, while its 72 logical bytes match. Disc 2 field 15 has the same class of boundary difference. Field component logical data, actor tables, collision structures and selected original code windows also pass direct source/RAM comparison.",
  "interpretation": "The eight-token decoder and field bundle require separate logical-file, physical-sector, decoded-output and original-memory-context bounds. Disc padding must not stand in for the original adjacent allocation. These measurements support a bounded source reconstruction and selected structures; they do not establish complete field formats or native gameplay.",
  "confidence": "supported",
  "validation": {
    "preconditions": [
      "Both supplied original CHDs and raw tracks pass the fresh exact-hash/container audit in .local/verification/phase1-20260908-sources/report.json.",
      "Use the pinned Nix observation-trace shell with its explicitly qualified HLE interpreter; retain original data locally.",
      "Each capture starts from reset through the existing recovered field loader, with no gameplay checkpoint.",
      "All outputs use new paths. The commands below were run for (disc,map)=(1,23),(1,14),(2,15); see each capture report for exact normalized scenario and program hashes."
    ],
    "commands": [
      "nix --extra-experimental-features \"nix-command flakes\" develop path:./nix#analysis -c chdman verify -i \"discs/Xenogears disc <disc>.chd\"",
      "python3 tools/analysis/verify_decoder.py prepare --raw .local/references/source-<disc>/disc.bin --profile <exact-profile> --map <map> --output <new-private-spec.json>",
      "python3 tools/reference/scenario.py <scenario> --content \"discs/Xenogears disc <disc>.chd\" --trace-instructions <new-private-spec.json> --output <new-private-run>",
      "python3 tools/analysis/verify_decoder.py compare --raw .local/references/source-<disc>/disc.bin --profile <exact-profile> --map <map> --capture <run>/capture --output <new-private-comparison.json>",
      "python3 tools/analysis/verify_field.py --raw .local/references/source-<disc>/disc.bin --profile <exact-profile> --map <map> --ram <run>/capture/final.ram --output <new-private-structures.json>",
      "python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -p test_field_analysis.py -v",
      "python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -p test_instruction_trace.py -v"
    ],
    "expected": "Original output memory hashes and CPU input/destination/return pointers at the decoder return are independent oracles. Reconstruction must match all bytes; matching logical prefixes cannot substitute for full output equality. Original unchanged source file hashes qualify each input; captured adjacent RAM qualifies out-of-file reads.",
    "actual": "27 complete outputs, totaling 374216 bytes, match exactly with measured input context. All three structural validations pass. Against prior uninstrumented cold boots, final 2 MiB RAM, external state, audio files and all 30 captured PNGs match exactly in all three cases. Synthetic tests exercise bounds only.",
    "result": "passed",
    "tolerance": "Exact hashes/bytes and register extents for these pinned HLE/interpreter runs; no hardware or native equivalence claim.",
